-- Transcription of layout-language-consult.md §5.5 (lines 588-599),
-- clean-room LengYue, portrait class. Disclosed adjustments beyond the
-- ones already covered in lengyue_landscape.lyt's header comment:
--   - `A_top[*, action]` uses '*' as a domain wildcard (the document's own
--     comment reads "A_go (+) A_common on one reserved strip", i.e. this
--     leaf merges two census domains into one strip). LYT's Domain type
--     has no wildcard/union member; we pick 'common' as the representative
--     domain, consistent with §4.3's own position that domain tagging is
--     advisory, not load-bearing for geometry.
--   - `I_engine[...]{28px, envelope as above}`: "as above" is prose
--     referencing §5.4's envelope states; spelled out explicitly here
--     rather than parsed literally (no such backreference exists in the
--     grammar).
--   - `T( tree, CP-* )[BLACK BOX]{pref 1fr, min 200px}` abbreviates the
--     black box further than §5.4 (bare `tree` with no bracket, and a
--     `CP-*` wildcard standing in for all five tabs). Expanded here to the
--     same six children as the landscape encoding — the census entities
--     are the same, only the prose shorthand differs — with each child's
--     own min set to 200px so the T node's structurally-derived min
--     (componentwise max of children, §4.1 line 298-302) reproduces the
--     document's explicit `min 200px` for the whole group.
--   - AMENDMENT 3 (ledger row 1715, gap-amendment-build): the root V(...)
--     gets `gap 12px`, `--space-medium` (`frontend/src/assets/css/
--     theme.css`'s own words: "section-level gap, content-block
--     separation"). Landscape's OUTER split uses the wider `--space-loose`
--     tier (20px) for its board-vs-side-column split, a clean two-way
--     major-region seam with generous width to spare; portrait's root
--     stacks bands in a narrower viewport, so the next tier down is the
--     disclosed, deliberate choice here, not an infeasibility workaround
--     (this class stayed OPTIMAL at `--space-loose` too when probed — see
--     build report). The new tree/panels/preview row below gets its own
--     `gap 4px` (`--space-tight`), matching landscape's identical row.
--
--   - TREE ALWAYS VISIBLE / boardRail / previewBoard (ledger row ~1735):
--     same three commissioner-driven changes as lengyue_landscape.lyt —
--     read that file's header in full for the shared rationale
--     (grounding citations, presence-menu mechanism disclosure, the
--     aspect-leaf generalization, the boardRail-as-popover open fork).
--     This file's own class-specific choices, not covered there:
--       - boardRail: the as-is app's 168px reservation is a WIDTH (a
--         left-edge rail column); portrait's root V partitions on
--         HEIGHT, so there is no literal "left edge" in a single-column
--         stack. Reinterpreted as a 168px-tall HORIZONTAL strip at the
--         TOP of the page (root V's new first child, before A_top) —
--         "top" being the portrait analog of "leftmost/first" in the
--         root's own child ORDER (matching the ruling's own "left edge
--         as today is the conservative choice": same numeric value,
--         same leading structural position, axis reinterpreted the way
--         every other shared-identity leaf in this pair of files already
--         is between classes). No stronger portrait-specific precedent
--         exists to ground a different number against — flagged as a
--         judgment call, not a re-derivation.
--       - previewBoard: reservation scaled DOWN from landscape's 160px to
--         96px (`min=pref=max=96px, aspect 1`) — "modest... scaled
--         sensibly to the region" (the ruling's own phrasing). Portrait's
--         tree/panels/preview row shares its width budget with the
--         tree's fixed 140px and the T node's 200px floor inside the
--         FULL VIEWPORT WIDTH (no elastic side-column buffer the way
--         landscape has); 96px is the down-scaled choice that keeps this
--         row's fixed+floor total (140+96+200=436px plus two 4px gaps)
--         comfortably under every representative portrait width this
--         prototype's own OVERLAY_SIZES table tests at 768px and up,
--         while genuinely tightening the narrowest two probes (540x960,
--         420x880) — see the build report's before/after feasibility
--         table for the measured outcome at each size, disclosed rather
--         than silently absorbed either way.
--
--   - AMENDMENT 4 (ledger row 1737, per-valuation presence solving,
--     SPEC-AMENDMENTS.md): boardRail and previewBoard below are now
--     genuinely `@toggle(user, release)` in this file's own concrete
--     syntax, same as lengyue_landscape.lyt — see that file's own
--     boardRail header note for the full rationale (the DEFAULT-OFF
--     state itself still lives at the registration layer, `runner.py`'s
--     `Registration.default_valuation`, not in this file's text).
--
--   - LYT TOOLBAR ONTOLOGY REENCODE (commissioner-ratified 2026-08-11,
--     ledger rows 1930/1931; `.claude/dispatch-reports/
--     lyt-toolbar-ontology-reencode.md`) — the commission's four points,
--     applied to THIS class: `A_top` is RENAMED `A_app[common, action]`
--     (same tree position, root child '1' — the widget id changes, the
--     structure doesn't) and `I_engine` is RENAMED `A_engine[go,
--     action+info]` (same tree position, root child '3'), now genuinely
--     `envelope: {disconnected, connected}` and MOUNTED for the first
--     time — portrait's own `I_engine` leaf previously mounted NOTHING
--     (disclosed W3 narrowing, `lyt-widget-registry.ts`'s prior
--     "class-scoped overrides" note: portrait's tree structurally
--     separated `I_engine` from `A_top`, so landscape's merged-Toolbar
--     disposition never carried over here). This reencode closes that
--     gap: portrait now has a REAL, working engine cluster it never had
--     before, not merely a rename. No path shift anywhere in this file
--     (unlike landscape, whose side column genuinely lost a V-child) —
--     portrait's own root V already kept `A_top`/`I_engine` as two
--     SEPARATE, non-adjacent children (the board composite sits between
--     them), so collapsing three leaves into two never applied here to
--     begin with. Reservations: `160px` (A_app) / `60px` (A_engine,
--     envelope-reserved) are a REAL Playwright measurement of the
--     realized components at portrait's own pinned representative
--     widths (420px — `tests/test_lyt.py`'s own
--     `test_lengyue_portrait_default_valuation_solves_optimal_at_420x880`;
--     1080px — `runner.py`'s own SCREEN_SIZES portrait point), taking
--     the worse (narrower, 420px) case per component plus a ~10px
--     margin — see the dispatch report's measurement table. Was `28px`
--     each (bare fixed shorthand) pre-reencode, a reservation this
--     encoding's own real content never actually fit inside even before
--     today (portrait's engine strip mounted nothing at all, and the
--     app strip's own real content already needed to wrap well past one
--     28px row) — this is a genuine, disclosed CORRECTION of an
--     under-measured prior value, not merely a resize for the new split.
--   - OPTION C TAB-SKELETON ENCODING (2026-08-11, ledger row 1937's
--     ratified consult; work item lyt-tab-skeleton-encoding). Same
--     re-homing + one-level-open shape as `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own
--     header note (read in full there for the grounding citations,
--     the settings-pane conservative-superset disclosure, the per-panel
--     height groundings/estimates, the CP-other L5c restructure, and the
--     BOTH-AXES TENSION note) — this class differs only in its
--     per-child `min` (200px, matching this file's own pre-existing
--     WRAPPER_MIN-analog convention, vs. landscape's 160px) for the two
--     still-opaque CP-library/CP-cards leaves; every genuinely NEW number
--     (the 838/664/204px composite floors, the per-panel floors) is
--     IDENTICAL across both classes — the underlying components render
--     the same regardless of screen orientation, so there is no honest
--     portrait-specific number to derive differently. Portrait's own
--     narrower available width makes the 838px settings floor and the
--     664px analysis floor considerably more likely to be the binding
--     constraint here than in landscape — reported, not pre-empted, in
--     the delivery report's solver results.
--
--     REPAIR (2026-08-11, `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-optionc-review.md`
--     Findings 2/3, corrected in `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-optionc-
--     repair.md`): same fixes as `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own header note
--     (read there for the full derivation) — the T(...)'s own wrapping
--     slot now carries an explicit `min 200px` (this file's own
--     pre-existing per-child marker reservation), so the emitter's
--     collapsed blackbox leaf reads that declared min directly instead of
--     re-deriving the solver's own componentwise-max floor from the (now
--     much deeper) composite children; and the settings-substrip demand
--     is corrected from the delivered wave's inflated 97ch/880px to the
--     actual 92ch/838px (a systematic +1-per-label ch-count error, five of
--     six labels affected — see the landscape header's Finding 3 note for
--     the full per-label table).
--
--     FLOW-CAPABLE SETTINGS SUBSTRIP (2026-08-11, work item
--     lyt-settings-live-opening, ledger rows 2007/2009): identical
--     derivation to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own header note (read there
--     in full — the six item widths, `research/lyt/flow.py`'s
--     `narrowest_width_for_row_count`/`flow_envelope`, the 2-row/443px/
--     60px design point, the BOTH-AXES-TENSION-driven composite min drop
--     from 838px to 443px). Applied identically here per this file's own
--     established convention (this section's own header line 120-121:
--     "every genuinely NEW number ... is IDENTICAL across both classes —
--     the underlying components render the same regardless of screen
--     orientation, so there is no honest portrait-specific number to
--     derive differently"). Portrait's own narrower available width
--     (line 122-126 above) means this correction is, if anything, MORE
--     load-bearing here than in landscape.
--
--     REPAIR (2026-08-12, independent review Finding 3 — identical
--     correction to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own REPAIR header note,
--     read there in full): `settingsSubstrip` moves `{60px}` -> `{77px}`
--     (the review's own live-measured 67px + this file's established
--     ~10px margin posture). Composite `min` unchanged at 443px (the new
--     281px height floor stays under the 443px width floor).
--
--   - M2 STAGE B2a (2026-08-12, ledger rows 2108/2331) — identical
--     rationale to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own M2 STAGE B2a header note
--     (read there in full for the fork-1 ruling, the L13/L16/L17 cascade
--     reasoning, and the `@demote` measurement basis); this class's own
--     numbers, where they differ:
--       - TREE BECOMES RESIDUAL-HOLDING: `tree` moves from
--         `{min 140px, pref 140px, max 140px}` to
--         `{min 140px, pref 1fr, max inf}` (its own established 140px
--         floor unchanged); `T(...)` is PINNED at `{min 664px, pref
--         664px, max 664px}` — the SAME 664px componentwise-max floor as
--         landscape (this file's own header, line 118-121: "every
--         genuinely NEW number... is IDENTICAL across both classes").
--       - L13/L16: `CP-library`/`CP-cards` gain `elastic h` + `floor v
--         200px` — 200px is this leaf's own already-declared `min` in
--         THIS file (line 116-117's own "200px, matching this file's own
--         pre-existing WRAPPER_MIN-analog convention"), not landscape's
--         160px.
--       - L17: direct load against this file finds `find_l17_violations`
--         fires at the same four sites as landscape (`CP-library`,
--         `CP-cards`, `settingsPane`, `otherBand`) — `boardRail`/`tree`
--         do not trip it here either, same correction as landscape's own
--         header note. `edge v item` (library/cards/settingsPane),
--         `edge v continuous` (otherBand) — same content-nature reasoning
--         as landscape.
--       - `@demote(h 616px)` on `A_app`: the measured threshold is
--         WIDTH-INVARIANT (identical at 1920 and 420 per the experiment
--         branch's own measurement, landscape header note above), so the
--         same 616px applies here. L15's own band-wide clause (b) cascade
--         is WIDER in this class: `A_app`'s own Split parent is the
--         ROOT `V(...)` itself (portrait has no separate side column —
--         `boardRail`, `A_app`, and `A_engine` are all THREE direct leaf
--         children of the same root split; the board composite and the
--         tree/panels row are composites, excluded), so all three need
--         `activity`. `A_engine` gains `activity sustained` (same
--         grounding as landscape). `boardRail` gains `activity
--         occasional` — grounded in its own product nature (an
--         open-boards navigation aid, already a default-OFF user toggle
--         per Amendment 4 — used when switching boards, not continuously
--         read the way the engine metrics are), distinct from landscape
--         where `boardRail` sits alone in the root `H`'s own split (no
--         other direct leaf child there) and so triggers no band-wide
--         cascade at all — an asymmetry between the two files driven
--         purely by tree shape, disclosed here rather than silently
--         matched. Verified directly: `find_l15_violations` returns `[]`
--         for every Split in this file's tree after these three
--         additions, and no other leaf anywhere in this file gains
--         `activity`.
--
--   - M2 STAGE B2b (2026-08-12, ledger rows 2073/2108/2151, the
--     ruling-basket census) -- identical rationale to
--     `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own M2 STAGE B2b header note (read there
--     in full for the three-vocabulary decomposition's per-group
--     grounding citations, the palette-adoption rationale/quotes, and
--     the settingsPane per-leaf §8.4 classification table); this
--     class's own differences, where they exist:
--
--     (1) ENGINE STATUS DECOMPOSITION -- identical shape
--     (`H(A_engine_controls, A_engine_eval, A_engine_health,
--     A_engine_queue)` replacing the bare `A_engine[go, action+info]`
--     leaf, SAME `{60px, envelope: {disconnected, connected}}` height
--     reservation on the wrapping `H(...)`, SAME undetermined per-group
--     width floor, filed the same frontier item). `activity sustained`
--     is RETIRED from this position the same way -- `A_engine` was the
--     ONE OTHER direct leaf child of the root `V(...)` this file's own
--     header note immediately above names as needing the band-wide
--     cascade; now that it is a composite, excluded, the root `V(...)`'s
--     own remaining direct leaf children needing `activity` are
--     `boardRail`/`A_app`/`A_setup` (item 2 below) -- THREE, not two,
--     the SAME "wider cascade in this class" shape the header note above
--     already documents, just with `A_setup` as the new third member
--     replacing `A_engine`'s own prior membership.
--
--     (2) PALETTE-AS-PRESENCE-SLOT -- identical `A_setup[common,
--     action]` leaf (`@toggle(user, release), {80px, content bounded,
--     activity occasional}`), placed as a direct ROOT `V(...)` child
--     (portrait has no separate side column -- same structural fact this
--     file's own header note above already establishes for `A_app`'s own
--     band-wide reach), positioned directly after `A_app` (the trigger's
--     own tree position, matching the palette's real in-flow docking
--     below its trigger). `runner.py`'s own `default_valuation` gains
--     `"A_setup"` for this class too (the SAME registration entry
--     already names both classes' widgets, since `default_valuation` is
--     declared once at the registration layer, not per-class).
--
--     (3) PANE GRANULARITY -- identical `T(SP_session, SP_analysisEnv,
--     SP_cardSets, SP_advancedRegistry, SP_analysis, SP_keybindings)`
--     shape, using this class's own already-established `200px` per-leaf
--     floor (this file's own OPTION C header note above: "this file's
--     own pre-existing WRAPPER_MIN-analog convention" -- 200px was
--     already this class's number for the analogous CP-library/CP-cards
--     floor, so no cross-class number choice was needed here the way
--     landscape's 160px-vs-200px distinction required its own header
--     note).
--
--     (4) ENGINE-ROW HEIGHT RE-GROUNDING (ledger row 2347, reviewer
--     finding 1) -- identical defect and identical fix to
--     `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own dated section of the same name
--     (read there for the full derivation: the retired merged
--     `ToolbarEngineCluster.vue`'s wrapping-H measurement carried
--     forward unexamined into item (1) above's decomposition,
--     `ToolbarEngineControls.vue`'s five buttons -- mint-card /
--     learn-path / play / match / connect-disconnect -- wrap to THREE
--     rows at the real post-decomposition column width, clipping Match
--     and Connect/Disconnect in the stale 60px track). MEASURED on the
--     SAME isolated rig, THIS class's own 768x1024 size (live column
--     width 189px): `.engine-controls` naturally needs **80px** (3
--     rows x 24px + 2 gaps x 4px), matching both the reviewer's own
--     finding and the landscape class's own 1920x1080 measurement
--     (197.5px column width) exactly -- the wrap count, not the column
--     width, is what changed between classes, and both land on the
--     same 3-row/80px shape. The other three groups checked the same
--     way (`.engine-metrics-bar`/`.queue-metric` declare no
--     `flex-wrap`, so neither can wrap regardless of width) and the
--     same STRUCTURAL LIMITATION applies (`H(...)` shares one
--     cross-axis fact across children; per-group heights are not
--     expressible without a tree restructure or new grammar, filed as
--     a frontier item, not undertaken here). Fix: raise the shared row
--     height from `60px` to `80px`, uniformly, same as landscape.
--
--   - MEASUREMENT-GROUNDED ENCODING PASS (2026-08-12) -- identical
--     rationale to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own header note of the same
--     name (read there in full: the isolated-rig methodology, the
--     CP-library/CP-cards unit values, the SP_advancedRegistry/
--     SP_keybindings non-uniform-pitch reasoning for why they stay
--     `item`, the timelineStrip full-grounding, and the A_setup 92px
--     re-grounding with its unattributed 12px delta) -- every number
--     this pass introduces is IDENTICAL across both classes (the same
--     live components render regardless of screen orientation, this
--     file's own established convention, see the OPTION C header note
--     above). This class's own difference: `CP-library`/`CP-cards`'
--     already-declared per-leaf `min` here is `200px` (this file's own
--     convention, not landscape's `160px`), still well over one whole
--     unit on the v axis for both the `32px`/`39px` units, so L10 is
--     satisfied the same way with a different (already-existing) min.
--
--   - LYT PRESENCE ARC P1 (2026-08-12, row 2333, mobile/portrait
--     repetition-first disposition; `.claude/dispatch-reports/
--     lyt-p1-presence-model.md`) -- identical CONTROL-PANEL DEMOTION
--     mechanism to `lengyue_landscape.lyt`'s own header note (read
--     there in full for the loader/presence.py widening this relies
--     on) -- this class's own threshold, re-derived from THIS file's
--     own named facts (identical derivation shape, different tree
--     position -- portrait has no side column, so the row is a direct
--     ROOT `V(...)` child):
--       664px (T's own pinned floor -- SAME 664px as landscape, M2
--         STAGE B2a above: "the SAME 664px componentwise-max floor as
--         landscape")
--     + 140px (tree's own floor, this file's own established
--         `TREE_PANEL_MIN_WIDTH_PX`, unchanged by W4 -- portrait-specific)
--     +   4px (one `--space-tight` row gap, this row's own already-
--         declared `gap 4px`, charged once -- previewBoard already
--         absent by default)
--     = 808px.
--
--     PORTRAIT REPETITION-FIRST DEFAULT (the second part of this arc,
--     distinct from landscape's diagnostic-only "demoted" coverage
--     point above): per the commissioner's own disposition (row 2333,
--     non-prescriptive but reasoned from here) -- mobile/portrait is
--     REPETITION-FIRST, board + match/play (the board composite,
--     `tree` navigation) primary, the control-panel tab group
--     (analysis graphs, browse tables, settings, debug -- every one of
--     `T(...)`'s five tabs) secondary -- `runner.py`'s own
--     `Registration.default_valuation_by_class["portrait"]` names
--     `"BLACK BOX"` (this Exclusive's own `[BLACK BOX]` tag, doubling
--     as its presence identity)
--     ABSENT alongside `boardRail`/`previewBoard`/`A_setup`, for
--     PORTRAIT ONLY (landscape's own `default_valuation` is untouched,
--     per row 2333's "do NOT shrink any desktop demand"). At every
--     portrait width narrower than 808px (768x1024, 540x960, 420x880
--     -- this repository's own three previously-INFEASIBLE `default`
--     representative points), the row's residual demand drops from
--     664+140+4=808px to just `tree`'s own 140px floor once T(...) is
--     pruned, which is what makes those three points genuinely
--     `OPTIMAL` under the new default (verified,
--     `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-p1-presence-model.md`'s own
--     before/after coverage-matrix table). `tree` itself is NOT
--     demoted -- it is the row's residual-holding sibling (Amendment 9,
--     M2 STAGE B2a) and the repetition-first disposition's own primary
--     surface (reviewing/replaying a game is match/play, not analysis).
--
--   - PORTRAIT ROW FLOOR, P2c (2026-08-12, ledger rows 2358/2359,
--     `.claude/dispatch-reports/lyt-p2c-portrait-row-floor.md`) -- the
--     defect P1's own item 3 diagnosed and disclosed as a recommendation,
--     not silently patched there: this row's own sizing bag, `{pref 1fr,
--     gap 4px} H(tree, T(...), previewBoard)`, declared no `min` of its
--     own. Since this row is a direct child of the root `V(...)` (portrait
--     has no side column, same structural fact the arc above already
--     names), its `min` is a HEIGHT floor along the root's own partition
--     axis -- and per SPEC.md §1.1's completion rule an undeclared `min`
--     defaults to `0px`, so nothing stopped board-maximize from squeezing
--     this row to a literal, honestly-reported zero once every sibling
--     had claimed its own share of the height budget (witnessed at
--     exactly 768x1024, P1's own item 3: `tree` rect `h=0`).
--
--     THE ARITHMETIC. Neither Amendment-8 key applies to this Split
--     child, so this is not a `floor v`/`min v` decision: `floor <axis>`
--     (L16) is LEAF-only (SPEC.md §16.1) and this row is an `H(...)`
--     Split, not a leaf; `min <axis>` (L12) is legal only at the root or
--     a direct child of an Exclusive/T node (SPEC.md §16.1) and this row
--     is a Split child of the root `V`, neither position. The construct
--     that DOES apply is the plain, un-axis-keyed `min` every node's own
--     sizing bag already carries (SPEC.md §4.1) -- the SAME idiom `tree`
--     itself already uses (`{min 140px, pref 1fr, max inf} tree[...]`,
--     two lines below), not a fresh grammar decision.
--
--     The number itself is `tree`'s OWN already-declared 140px floor
--     (`TREE_PANEL_MIN_WIDTH_PX`, the arc above's own named fact),
--     reused cross-axis rather than freshly invented (row 2047's own "a
--     decision posed in pixels is a defect" discipline): under this
--     row's own `default`/`demoted` valuations, `T(...)` and
--     `previewBoard` are BOTH absent (the repetition-first arc above),
--     so `tree` is the row's SOLE, residual-holding content
--     (Amendment 9, SPEC.md §17) at those points -- there is no OTHER
--     child whose own declared facts could honestly ground this row's
--     height floor instead. Squeezing the row below 140px squeezes
--     `tree` below the SAME number this file already treats as "not
--     usefully visible" on its other axis, so reusing it here (rather
--     than picking an unrelated fresh constant) is the reservation-not-
--     measurement posture SPEC.md §4.2 already commits this language to,
--     applied across axes rather than inventing a second number for the
--     same "meaningfully visible" judgment. Disclosed, not a rigorous
--     componentwise-max derivation the way `T(...)`'s own 664px is (no
--     such rule exists for a Split's along-axis `min` against its
--     children's cross-axis facts) -- the honest anchor available, named
--     as such rather than dressed up as more derived than it is.
--
--     Feasibility checked, not assumed: `coverage_matrix.py` before/after
--     re-solve finds every portrait point that was `OPTIMAL` before this
--     edit stays `OPTIMAL` after (768x1024's own `tree`/row height rises
--     from the degenerate `0px` to a genuine `140px`; the other four
--     portrait representative points were already at or above 140px and
--     are unaffected) -- see the dispatch report for the full before/
--     after table.
layout lengyue-portrait =
  {min 0px, pref 1fr, max inf, gap 12px} V(
    @toggle(user, release) {min 168px, pref 168px, max 168px, activity occasional} boardRail[common, info+action],
    @demote(h 616px) {160px, content bounded, activity occasional} A_app[common, action],
    @toggle(user, release) {92px, content bounded, activity occasional} A_setup[common, action],
    {pref 1fr} V(
      {width 100fr, aspect 1} B[board],
      {24px} I_board[board, info],
      {28px} A_board[board, action]
    ),
    {80px, envelope: {disconnected, connected}, gap 4px} H(
      {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_controls[go, action],
      {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_eval[go, info],
      {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_health[go, info],
      {pref 1fr, content bounded} A_engine_queue[go, info]
    ),
    {min 140px, pref 1fr, gap 4px} H(
      {min 140px, pref 1fr, max inf} tree[board, info+action],
      @demote(h 808px) {min 664px, pref 664px, max 664px} T(
        {min 200px, pref 1fr, max inf, boundary, content unbounded, scroll v, elastic h, floor v 200px, edge v unit, unit v 32px} CP-library[common],
